Z||000000||fierodave||08-27-2001||07:33 PM||||<BR>87 GT~ 60k original miles.   <BR>Fresh from the Paint booth. <BR>Wet sanded & buffed.  Ready for delivery to the happy owner.<BR>I am heading to Milwaukee in the Am to drop this one off. If you need anything down that way, I need to know before midnight tonight!<BR>Thanks for the space,<BR>FD<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=101570&a=13666063&p=53256387&Sequence=4&res=high"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=101570&a=13666063&p=53454408&Sequence=4&res=high"> <P>More pic's <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=101570&a=13666063" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=101570&a=13666063</A> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Urchin||08-27-2001||07:35 PM||||Wow, does that ever look nice!   If they're not happy with it let me know, and I'll take it off your hands   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_cut_sig_4.jpg">   <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.<p>[This message has been edited by Urchin (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||CoolBlue87GT||08-27-2001||08:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierodave:<BR><B>Ready for delivery to the happy owner.<BR>I am heading to Milwaukee in the Am to drop this one off</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>When you get back, let me know how that dolly worked out.<P>I've been thinking about using one of those next time.  I've rented an auto trailers in the past, it was 2100 lbs empty. My Cherokee was near it's limit with both car & trailer.<P>I'd like to know how it tracked behind the tow vehicle.  Did it fishtail at all ?<P>I noticed you have it loaded backwards. Is that better than forwards ?<P>Is it hard to load / unload ?  I've been told its hard to backup with those.<P>Thanks for any info.  The car looks great !<BR>How long did that take ? Good luck on the trip.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000003||fierodave||08-27-2001||09:56 PM||||This dolly has pulled over 150 Fiero's since last November, One all the way back from Ca. to Wi. with out a care in the world. There is<BR>No fishtailing at all!  If someone says they have that problem, they either don't know how to drive or have bad towing equipment! <BR>I use a old 85 Ford F-150 6 cyl 2 wheel drive pick up and have logged about 6,000 miles on it in the last three months.  Make sure the tires on the towed & tow vehicle are inflated properly.  I load all of them this way (backwards) It works better for me!  You can pull a stick car front on first anywhere you want all day long, I just load them all this way, my personal preference is all.   It's Not hard to load at all!<BR>just back it on, or use a winch if the car does not run. Tug it on the dolly and drive it off to unload it. •••••YOU CANNOT•••• backup a dolly! It WILL cause damage to the unit!<P>How long did the car take to do?  <BR>It took about 40-45 hours on this one plus my tow time (16 hours) to pick it up and deliver it.<BR>FD<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by fierodave (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||1
